hadiths[26]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3764","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: She (the narrator says) i.e. Sayyida Barira (may Allah be pleased with her) was given authority, her husband was a slave."
"3765","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave."
"3766","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her authority. Her husband was a slave."
"3767","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave. Sheikh Abu Bakr Neshapuri says: This hadith is poor."
"3768","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Barira's husband was a slave."
"3769","Nafi, narrates this statement of Sayyida Safiyyah bint Abu Ubaid (may God be pleased with her) that Barira's husband was a slave."
"3770","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given this decision about Barira: She was the wife of a slave."
"3771","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave."
"3772","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Barira's husband was a black slave of Banumaghira. By Allah, I still remember the scene well on the day when Barira was freed."
"3773","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: When Berirah was given authority, I saw her husband walking behind her in the streets of Madinah, his tears were flowing down his beard. Allah you are ordering me? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “No, I am only recommending. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave authority to this woman and she adopted her own self."
"3774","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When Barirah was given authority, her husband was a slave of Banu Mughira."
"3775","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Barira if he had intercourse with you (after you were freed), you will not have authority. In the tradition of Ibn Mujahid, there are these words: If he gets close to you, you will not have authority."
"3776","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When Barira separated from her husband, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed her Idda as that of a divorced woman (which means three menstrual periods)."
"3777","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) freed Barirah from being married and set the conditions for her marriage, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision: the freedman has the right to marry her. (As much as) appointed. Some narrators have quoted these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed her to observe the Iddah."
"3778",": Ubaidah says about this verse: \And if you are afraid of fighting among yourselves"," send a mediator from the family of the man and a mediator from the family of the woman.\"" (Ubaidah narrates:) A man and a woman came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and each of them was accompanied by some people. Sayyidna Ali (RA) instructed them to appoint an arbitrator from the man's family and an arbitrator from the woman's family. It is obligatory upon you that if you think that there should be a separation between the two of them"," then you separate them. Then the woman said: I am satisfied with the decision of the Book of Allah regarding the payment that is required of me and the right that I have to get (i.e. I am ready to accept it). You also have to confess what this woman has done."""
"3779","Ubaidah narrates: A man and a woman came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and there were some people with them. When Sayyidna Ali (RA) appointed the two as arbitrators, he said: Wait now, I will tell you what is required of you. Do you know what is required of you? Sayyiduna Ali (RA) turned to the woman and said: Will you agree with what these two decide? The woman replied, \Yes"," I agree with the decision of Allah's book regarding what is imposed on me and what I get.\"" Then Sayyiduna Ali turned to the man and said"," \""Will you agree with what these two arbitrators decide?\"" He replied no"," if they decide to keep both of them together"," then I agree"," and if they decide to separate"," then I will not agree"," then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said to him"," you have said wrong: By Allah"," you will have to agree in the same way as this woman is agreeing to her."""
"3780","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The best charity is that which is given in the world of prosperity (i.e., after giving charity, the person himself is not poor) and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. The narrator narrates: I said, O Messenger of Allah! Who is my guardian? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Your wife who says"," \""Give me something to eat"," otherwise divorce me.\"""""
"3781","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A woman will say to her husband: Give me food, otherwise divorce me. The man's slave will say: First, give me food, then take work from me, and the children will say: To whom are you leaving me?"
"3782","Saeed bin Musaib says about a person who is unable to pay the expenses of his wife, he says: If that person is unable to pay the khach, then the husband and wife will be separated."
"3783","Saeed bin Musayyib says about a person who is unable to pay his wife's expenses: Separation will be made between these husband and wife."
"3784","The same has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira."
"3785","Ishaq bin Bahlul says: He said to Abdullah bin Dawud: If a man does not find a relation of the same family for a girl under his care, should he marry her to a pious person (of a lesser family)? So he replied, Sayyiduna Umar (RA) says: I will allow women from good families to marry only in the same family."
"3786","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take righteous places (i.e. righteous wives) for your sperm."
"3787","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Get married in Kufu and get them married, take (righteous wives) for your sperm, and avoid Abyssinians, because their outward appearance is not good."
"3788","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the best (i.e. good wives) for your sperm and keep it only in Kafu. A narrator named Ashaj has narrated these words: Take the best (i.e. good wives) for your offspring and marry them in Kafu, and marry them (the Kafu)."
"3789","Sufyan says: Kafu will be considered according to customs and religion."
